######################################################################
# Build context exclusions for the Docker image.
#
# Anything matched here is NOT sent to the Docker daemon, which makes
# `transferring context` faster and prevents stale local artifacts from
# leaking into the image.
######################################################################

# --- VCS / editor metadata -----------------------------------------------
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.history
*.swp

# --- Local Node / build output (rebuilt inside the image) ---------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
build
coverage
.cache
.turbo
.parcel-cache
.next
.vite

# --- Logs / runtime junk ------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.npm
.yarn
.pnpm-store

# --- Environment / secrets ---------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Agent metadata ----------------------------------------------------
.local
.agents
attached_assets/Pasted-*
attached_assets/image_*
attached_assets/screenshots
attached_assets/quarantine

# --- Test artefacts not needed in the runtime image --------------------
# NOTE: docs/ and *.md are intentionally NOT excluded here. The Docker
# `builder` stage runs `npm run build`, which chains
# `npm run lint:version` (task-465 / task-467). That lint walks the
# repo to verify every @managed-version doc marker matches version.json
# AND that update-version.sh's MANAGED_DOCS array still corresponds to
# files that exist on disk. Excluding docs from the builder context
# made the lint report 10 MANAGED_DOCS entries as "missing" inside
# Docker (task-473), failing the deploy. The runtime stage never does
# `COPY .` — it cherry-picks dist/, shared/, migrations/, etc. — so
# letting docs into the builder does NOT add docs to the runtime image.
#
# That "runtime stage stays clean" invariant is actively enforced by
# scripts/verify-no-internal-docs.sh, which the Dockerfile runtime
# stage runs as a bind-mounted RUN step (task-474). If anyone later
# adds a `COPY . .` or `COPY docs/` to the runtime stage, the docker
# build fails with a clear error before the image is published.
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx

# --- OS junk -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
